<section class="section section-tint" id="refugee" aria-labelledby="refugee-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row g-5">
      <div class="col-lg-7 prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Refugee vaccination documentation</p>
        <h2 id="refugee-heading">Vaccination documentation for refugee applicants</h2>
        <p>Certain refugees applying for adjustment of status may need only the vaccination portion of Form I-693 completed, rather than a full immigration medical examination. Glah Medical Group offers vaccination record reviews and completion of the applicable vaccination documentation for eligible individuals.</p>
        <p><strong>Please contact our office to determine whether you qualify for this type of appointment.</strong></p>
        <p>This limited vaccination assessment is for refugees adjusting status. It does not automatically apply to everyone with refugee or asylum-related status. Derivative asylees generally have different requirements.</p>
        <h3 class="h4">What is different for this appointment</h3>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>You complete only <strong>pages 1&ndash;5 and 12&ndash;14</strong> of Form I-693.</li>
          <li>You must have <strong>documentation showing that you are a refugee</strong>.</li>
          <li>Cost: <strong>{{ pricing.refugeeVaccination }}</strong>, including the physical and completion of the form. Payment is cash, debit card or credit card.</li>
          <li>Appointments are at our <strong>Camp Hill office</strong>, 797 Poplar Church Road. The sign says &ldquo;Hampden Surgeons/Glah Medical Group.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-5">
        <aside class="values-card mb-4" aria-labelledby="refugee-bring-heading">
          <h2 id="refugee-bring-heading" class="h4">What to bring</h2>
          <ol class="ps-3 mb-0">
            <li>Any documents from USCIS showing your status as a refugee</li>
            <li>Government-issued photo ID, such as a valid passport or driver's license</li>
            <li>Your vaccination or immunization record</li>
            <li>Payment: cash, debit card or credit card</li>
            <li>Your printed Form I-693, pages 1&ndash;5 and 12&ndash;14 only. <a href="{{ links.uscisI693Pdf }}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Download the form from USCIS<span class="visually-hidden"> (PDF, opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>
          </ol>
        </aside>
        <aside class="values-card mb-4" aria-labelledby="refugee-form-heading">
          <h2 id="refugee-form-heading" class="h4">Filling out your form</h2>
          <ul class="check-list mb-0">
            <li>Use <strong>black ink</strong> and write in <strong>ALL CAPITAL LETTERS</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Page 1:</strong> fill in the whole page.</li>
            <li><strong>Page 2:</strong> print your last, first and middle name at the top, and fill in your phone number and email address.</li>
            <li><strong>Top of each remaining page:</strong> print your last, first and middle name in the spaces provided.</li>
            <li>Leave the applicant, interpreter and preparer signature and date sections blank until your appointment.</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
